    "contract": "assurance_kernel/task_intent/v1",
    "task_id": "loop-sched-s4-interaction-local",
    "goal": "Add the local Interaction channel: the daemon writes requests under its state directory, every Host lists them through loop_interactions and answers them only through the privileged answer_loop_interaction tool's native confirmation, selected by loop.interaction.channel, per D4 of docs/specs/loop-agent-scheduling.spec.md.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "S4-AC1",
        "assertion": "Source BR-DEC-7, BR-SCN-2; meet D4 in docs/specs/loop-agent-scheduling.spec.md. Agreed seam: tests/loop-sched-interaction-local.test.ts over the local channel, the shared MCP tool runtime and the Pi tool registration. Done looks like: with loop.interaction.channel local, a pending Lane decision appears in loop_interactions, an answer confirmed through answer_loop_interaction is applied through the Lane decision relay and the Lane continues on the next tick. Negative: an answer file without the privileged tool's confirmation record is ignored; an answer to a stale request is refused; a plan_approval request is never answered by the tool and points to drive. Bound: loop.interaction.channel other than github or local is config_invalid; absent means github.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v2\",\n  \"command\": {\n    \"executable\": \"bun\",\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"test\",\n      \"tests/loop-sched-interaction-local.test.ts\",\n      \"tests/layered-config.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"cwd\": \".\",\n    \"timeout_ms\": 180000,\n    \"max_output_bytes\": 131072\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"prepare\": null,\n    \"writable_paths\": []\n  }\n}\n"
      }
